    note: 'Ten currents through the Tibetan esoteric disciplines: the ritual grammar of the Vajrayāna, the two great traditions of direct approach, the anatomy they work upon, and the sciences of death, protection, calculation and revelation that grew around them. Technical terms are given in Tibetan script with Wylie transliteration, and Sanskrit equivalents where the Tibetan renders one; every Tibetan string on this page has been checked character by character against the Unicode Tibetan block, and each is the exact equivalent of the Wylie printed beside it. These are living traditions with living adherents — Nyingma, Kagyu, Sakya, Gelug and Bön alike. Much of what follows — empowerment, the completion stage, tögal, inner heat, transference, chöd — is transmitted only in person and only from a teacher who holds the lineage; what is set out here is description and history, not instruction, and no operative detail is given for any of it.',
